WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:05.462
Night two. Six nights left to bring a runaway dream home.

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:17.151
Theo? What are you doing here?

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:24.046
You saw the singing snow too. I'm coming with you. No arguments.

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:29.049
So… where exactly are we going?

00:00:31.437 --> 00:00:34.009
Somewhere you won't believe.

00:00:48.437 --> 00:00:51.009
Okay. Okay. I believe you.

00:00:52.277 --> 00:00:57.017
You brought a friend. The Archive does not usually allow guests.

00:01:01.717 --> 00:01:07.006
But the jars are humming for him. So… welcome, young man.

00:01:12.017 --> 00:01:16.993
If you are going to help, you must know the three rules of the Archive.

00:01:18.437 --> 00:01:23.021
Rule one. Never open a jar that is not yours.

00:01:24.947 --> 00:01:28.016
It opened by itself. I promise.

00:01:28.857 --> 00:01:36.001
Rule two. A dream outside its jar grows weaker in daylight. And stranger.

00:01:36.867 --> 00:01:40.014
Stranger like… singing snow?

00:01:41.577 --> 00:01:47.989
Exactly like that. Rule three. Never let the Shadow catch a dream.

00:01:49.227 --> 00:01:53.001
The man in the hat. I saw him on the school roof.

00:01:59.697 --> 00:02:06.997
He collects lost dreams and silences them. If he catches yours, it is gone forever.

00:02:12.527 --> 00:02:18.156
Every jar is written here. Whose dream it is, and when it was dreamed.

00:02:24.417 --> 00:02:28.766
Someone tore it out. The name for our jar is missing.

00:02:31.147 --> 00:02:33.641
Please tell me the Shadow can't read.

00:02:36.177 --> 00:02:38.984
It's ringing. The dream is close!

00:02:44.767 --> 00:02:48.227
Careful! Stay where the jars are bright!

00:02:57.067 --> 00:03:00.998
Hey… it's okay. I'm not going to hurt you.

00:03:14.067 --> 00:03:17.998
I… I know this. I've seen this before.

00:03:26.857 --> 00:03:29.037
Mira. Behind us.

00:03:29.897 --> 00:03:33.984
Away from them! The children are under my protection!

00:03:40.967 --> 00:03:45.472
Five nights left. And Mira was beginning to remember.

